cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "whisper-tiny vs whisper-base in a browser tab: word error rate, timing, transfer size and peak memory"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Clipquill"
    website: "https://clipquill.com"
date-released: "2026-09-18"
version: 1.0.0
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/supersophia8888-cloud/clipquill-asr-benchmark"
url: "https://clipquill.com"
abstract: >-
  Measurements of two quantised Whisper tiers (onnx-community/whisper-tiny and
  onnx-community/whisper-base) running client-side in a real Chrome window.
  Word error rate on eight clips across five acoustic conditions (229 reference
  words), wall-clock timing on byte-identical audio from 13 to 1610 seconds,
  per-file transfer size of the model as served, peak resident memory of the
  browser process tree, browser decodability of eight container formats, and a
  single-clip Mandarin character error rate at three normalization levels.
keywords:
  - speech recognition
  - whisper
  - word error rate
  - browser
  - wasm
  - onnx
  - benchmark
  - client-side inference
